{% comment %}
  The country list the location picker shows — rendered twice, once in the
  desktop drawer and once inside the mobile menu, so the two never drift.

  Every country Shopify offers is here: the store serves 215 of them across
  its markets, most through the International market. A list that long is
  read by typing, so a filter sits above it; the filter is JavaScript's and
  the list is complete without it. A country is a BUTTON rather than a link:
  the click sets the localization form's country and submits it, and there
  is no page a link could honestly point at. What the row prints is
  Shopify's own name for the country, in the language the visitor is
  reading — the same word the footer's selector would use.

  Accepts: suffix — a short word making the ids unique per render.
{% endcomment %}
{%- liquid
  assign suffix = suffix | default: 'list'
  assign current_iso = localization.country.iso_code
-%}
<div class="st-location__list" data-location-list>
  <label class="st-location__filter" for="StLocationFilter-{{ suffix }}">
    <span class="visually-hidden">{{ 'localization.find_country' | t }}</span>
    <input
      type="search"
      id="StLocationFilter-{{ suffix }}"
      class="st-location__filter-input"
      placeholder="{{ 'localization.find_country' | t }}"
      autocomplete="off"
      autocorrect="off"
      autocapitalize="off"
      spellcheck="false"
      data-location-filter
    >
  </label>
  <ul class="st-location__countries list-unstyled" role="list">
    {%- for c in localization.available_countries -%}
      <li class="st-location__item" data-location-item data-name="{{ c.name | downcase | escape }} {{ c.iso_code | downcase }}">
        <button
          type="button"
          class="st-location__country{% if c.iso_code == current_iso %} is-current{% endif %}"
          data-location-pick="{{ c.iso_code }}"
          {% if c.iso_code == current_iso %}aria-current="true"{% endif %}
        >{{ c.name }}</button>
      </li>
    {%- endfor -%}
  </ul>
  <p class="st-location__none" data-location-none hidden>{{ 'localization.no_match' | t }}</p>
</div>
